But Tim Wong, Jonah T, Addie H, and Kiana Raber also wrote in about Randall's hand.

1991
00:55:39.620 --> 00:55:41.300
Well, great job, guys.

1992
00:55:41.440 --> 00:55:41.960
Great job.

1993
00:55:42.220 --> 00:55:47.380
We also had Jasper Anders and Morgan Elridge write in to ask,

1994
00:55:47.940 --> 00:55:53.000
what did Phil Shea use for the bird eggs that Dwight finds and cooks?

1995
00:55:53.260 --> 00:55:56.200
They kind of look like they might be small potatoes.

1996
00:55:56.620 --> 00:55:57.420
Guess what?

1997
00:55:57.980 --> 00:55:58.420
What?

1998
00:55:58.960 --> 00:56:00.480
They were small potatoes.

1999
00:56:01.180 --> 00:56:01.680
Really?

2000
00:56:02.140 --> 00:56:05.020
Teeny tiny potatoes meant to look like eggs.

2001
00:56:05.320 --> 00:56:09.180
I totally thought they were eggs, but I was trying to think what kind of bird

2002
00:56:09.180 --> 00:56:11.100
makes a nest like that up in a tree.

2003
00:56:13.070 --> 00:56:13.590
What?

2004
00:56:16.290 --> 00:56:17.210
Many birds?

2005
00:56:17.970 --> 00:56:18.810
So many birds?

2006
00:56:19.070 --> 00:56:20.930
That was such a big nest, though.

2007
00:56:21.170 --> 00:56:24.430
Like, those eggs look like a bird that would, like, lay them on the ground to me.

2008
00:56:26.110 --> 00:56:29.990
Or, I mean, I guess, what?

2009
00:56:32.700 --> 00:56:37.600
Or maybe they're the eggs of a bird that would nest really up high.

2010
00:56:38.060 --> 00:56:38.460
Exactly.

2011
00:56:38.880 --> 00:56:41.880
They didn't look like the type of eggs that you could just reach with your hand.

2012
00:56:42.060 --> 00:56:45.440
I think you would either find them on the ground or they'd be up on a clifftop.

2013
00:56:45.660 --> 00:56:48.080
I think that that's a good way to say it.

2014
00:56:50.320 --> 00:56:55.360
When you said, what kind of bird lays eggs in a tree?

2015
00:56:56.500 --> 00:56:57.880
I was confused.

2016
00:56:58.160 --> 00:56:58.700
This is my mom.

2017
00:56:58.700 --> 00:57:02.480
But I'm hearing your point now, and I hear it, and I think it's a good point.

2018
00:57:03.000 --> 00:57:03.400
Thank you.

2019
00:57:03.580 --> 00:57:08.920
I need to talk about this shot of Michael singing happy birthday, because it is just wonderful.

2020
00:57:09.400 --> 00:57:09.620
Oh.

2021
00:57:09.820 --> 00:57:11.620
Michael has just made a spear.

2022
00:57:12.020 --> 00:57:16.640
The teeniest, tiniest spear on the end of a very crooked stick.

2023
00:57:16.640 --> 00:57:24.400
I want to point out that he made a spear when he has an amazing knife, like you would think he would attach the knife to the end of the stick.

2024
00:57:24.640 --> 00:57:25.920
With his duct tape.

2025
00:57:26.020 --> 00:57:26.860
With his duct tape.

2026
00:57:27.420 --> 00:57:32.480
He might have used all his duct tape to fashion his tent out of his pants.

2027
00:57:32.480 --> 00:57:33.940
That's coming up, I guess.

2028
00:57:34.100 --> 00:57:38.620
But, yeah, there's this shot that pulls so far back.

2029
00:57:38.620 --> 00:57:50.140
And what's amazing about it to me is, guys, Steve was really in the middle of nowhere, and our crew was far back as this shot reveals.

2030
00:57:50.860 --> 00:57:51.060
Yeah.

2031
00:57:51.400 --> 00:57:53.240
I thought it was a beautiful shot.

2032
00:57:53.240 --> 00:58:03.580
I also love these moments when Michael remembers things like sprinkles, like Creed's birthday, you know, when he sings a song and he's like, happy birthday, buddy.

2033
00:58:04.120 --> 00:58:04.300
Yeah.

2034
00:58:04.600 --> 00:58:06.760
These are those very sweet Michael moments.

2035
00:58:06.760 --> 00:58:12.220
This shot also made me think about how Steve Carell wrote this episode.

2036
00:58:12.400 --> 00:58:17.340
He wrote himself a very difficult shoot day out in the woods.

2037
00:58:17.400 --> 00:58:20.060
He did, where he gets tackled by Dwight.

2038
00:58:20.220 --> 00:58:21.340
Oh, my gosh.

2039
00:58:21.560 --> 00:58:33.200
If I were writing an episode for myself, I would make it pajama day at the office, where we all wear our pajamas, and there are no stunts.

2040
00:58:34.120 --> 00:58:37.300
I would write a very different episode.

2041
00:58:37.300 --> 00:58:41.840
So I applaud Steve for really going for it in the name of comedy.

2042
00:58:42.140 --> 00:58:46.440
Back in the office, we have bitching in the break room.

2043
00:58:46.640 --> 00:58:47.620
Oh, I love this.

2044
00:58:47.820 --> 00:58:53.760
Everyone is in the break room, and they are complaining about Jim's new birthday ordinance.

2045
00:58:54.120 --> 00:58:55.960
And it's just a gripe feSt.

2046
